HST Office: Sheets opens an .xlsx with many cell formats faster: no copy of every style's ranges per lookup.

SheetDataBuffer::addColXfStyles groups the imported cell ranges by equal Xf. addIfNotInMyMap looks for an entry
with std::find_if over a std::map<FormatKeyPair, ScRangeList>, but its lambda took
const std::pair<FormatKeyPair, ScRangeList>&: the map's value_type has a const key, so every visited entry was
converted into a temporary pair, copying its whole ScRangeList, for every key looked up. Profiled on the 50 MB
xlsx-formats fixture (Linux, 1.0.2): ScRangeList's copy constructor plus its memmove/malloc were about a quarter of
all samples of the sheet import thread. The lambda now takes the map's value_type; nothing else changes (the same
entries are compared in the same order).

License: this upstream file remains under its original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: build; CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_filters_test2 (xlsx import with styles) unchanged; open-time before/after
with scripts/perf/large-file-open.py on xlsx-formats-50mb.
---
